1
00:00:00,354 --> 00:00:06,554
Diabetic eye disease is the top cause of blindness in working-age adults. One in four people with diabetes has it,

2
00:00:06,607 --> 00:00:11,547
yet a third skip their yearly exam, and most photos of the eye end up as a line in a chart.

3
00:00:12,154 --> 00:00:22,694
I'm Aasrith Mandava from team CodePaws. At HackGT 13 we built Insight Rx: one photo of the eye becomes what to treat, which drug to target, and who to call.

4
00:00:23,298 --> 00:00:31,008
It's built for healthcare providers, or HCPs: the family doctor decides in the visit; the specialist gets a complete, signed consult.

5
00:00:31,062 --> 00:00:36,132
Drug makers reach the right HCP when therapy is decided, with no cold outreach.

6
00:00:36,738 --> 00:00:44,318
Under the hood: a web app on Vercel and Neon, our AI on a live GPU through a Cloudflare tunnel, and five smart services.

7
00:00:44,924 --> 00:00:50,684
Every role has its own login and sees only what it should. I'm Dr. Alex Morgan, a family doctor.

8
00:00:51,037 --> 00:00:56,837
I add a phone photo of each eye, the age and current medicines, and send them to our GPU model.

9
00:00:57,815 --> 00:01:05,075
It builds on DINOv2, a vision AI trained on millions of images, fine-tuned to read retinas. Here's where it looked.

10
00:01:05,128 --> 00:01:12,778
After a quality check: disease needing a specialist, in both eyes. Shown a sick and a healthy eye, it's right 98 times in 100.

11
00:01:13,383 --> 00:01:19,393
Eye vessels mirror the body, so a second model flags heart, kidney and nerve risks, each with a trust label.

12
00:01:19,999 --> 00:01:26,839
Guideline treatments are checked against current medicines, catching two eye-specific risks: semaglutide and pioglitazone.

13
00:01:27,445 --> 00:01:36,875
Next, it ranks the proteins behind this disease by evidence, guidelines and drug-site certainty. Top pick: VEGF-A, which makes vessels leak.

14
00:01:42,663 --> 00:01:49,863
Flip to DeepMind's AlphaFold: the drug touches 21 spots, and AlphaFold is 95 out of 100 confident about them.

15
00:01:50,471 --> 00:01:55,701
Across patients, the explorer shows drug makers where eye-detected demand meets few existing drugs.

16
00:01:56,306 --> 00:02:07,076
Now the HCP-to-HCP handoff: one click saves the patient and opens a consult. Confirm, pick a specialist, sign, sealed with a SHA-256 fingerprint.

17
00:02:10,277 --> 00:02:14,597
The retina specialist accepts it, and the next step passes to the care coordinator.

18
00:02:17,181 --> 00:02:22,401
Outside the network? Real doctors from the national NPI registry, with a referral letter.

19
00:02:23,006 --> 00:02:29,816
When an HCP asks a drug maker a question, a firewall shows them an age range and findings, never the patient.

20
00:02:31,433 --> 00:02:37,963
The Copilot looks up guidelines first, then Gemini writes a cited answer, and Backboard's memory keeps it true to my habits.

21
00:02:40,390 --> 00:02:48,590
Gemini rewrites the result in plain words in the patient's own language, never adding numbers or names, and ElevenLabs' multilingual voice reads it aloud.

22
00:02:52,364 --> 00:02:57,934
Every screening feeds a Tiger Data time-series database that rolls findings up daily, automatically.

23
00:02:58,539 --> 00:03:05,499
And it pays for itself: each screen read by a doctor closes a Medicare quality gap and bills code 92228.

24
00:03:06,105 --> 00:03:11,655
Every action lands in a tamper-evident audit trail, ready to stamp its fingerprint on the Solana blockchain.

25
00:03:12,258 --> 00:03:22,128
Per ten thousand patients: about 3,500 missed exams closed, $300,000 in billable reads, and 2,600 people with eye disease found.

26
00:03:22,731 --> 00:03:31,411
Gemini explains, ElevenLabs speaks, Backboard remembers, Tiger Data tracks, Solana keeps records honest, and Grok voiced this video.

27
00:03:32,017 --> 00:03:39,867
Insight Rx: HCP engagement, triggered by a clinical signal. One eye photo, the right treatment, the right doctor.

